<title>UK: UK unions &quot;in dispute&quot; with Ford.</title>
<headline>UK unions &quot;in dispute&quot; with Ford.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British union workers are &quot;in dispute&quot; with Ford unless the U.S. car company reverses its decision to axe 1,300 jobs at the Halewood plant in northwest England, a top union officer said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have told them we are in dispute unless and until they reverse their disgraceful decision to close Halewood,&quot; said Tony Woodley, national officer with the Transport and General Workers Union.</p>
<p>Woodley spoke after union chiefs held talks with Ford management over its decision to axe the jobs at the plant, which produces Escort cars for the domestic market.</p>
</text>
